We all know that scumsaving is considered an abuse.  One doesn't post
YAAP if they've lost a character then restored him/her from a save file
-- it's cheating.

However, restoring from a backup is not ALWAYS cheating. I keep a
backup file or two in case of power failure -- the idea being, if the
death happens in-game, the character is dead -- but I'm not giving up a
promising character just because a fellow housemate shut the game down
while I was using the restroom, or the power died, or a parakeet landed
on the keyboard, or ...

However, there is a gray area.

Fairly frequently, my character is in Sokoban.  While he is busy
shovin' boulders around,  the RNG will randomly generate a character in
a bottleneck corridor *between* the pits and the rock
I am currently pushing.

There is no way to get to the critter, because it's trapped between the
pit and the boulder.


What I would like to do is shut down and restart from the beginning of
the level, on the grounds that I shouldn't take a luck hit I am not
responsible for and could not have prevented.

Is this acceptable? Or is it an abuse?  I'll certainly take the luck
hit if I bobbled the maze, but it doesn't seem quite right for me to
need to pickaxe or dig my way through a rock (for a luck hit), kill the
monster, and if I'm low on rock have to read a scroll of earth for an
even bigger luck hit, then plunk the boulder into place.  Why go
through all this trouble when there's no way a kobold without
levitation could magically appear between the rock and the pit?

